# Copy to `.env.local` (or set the variables in the deployment environment).
#
# The author app lives on its own origin, so every shell link has to point back
# at the public site. `PUBLIC_SITE_ORIGIN` is the single configurable target:
# https for production, or http://localhost for development. It is public data,
# never a secret. These values are read at build time by `vite.config.ts`.
#
# Development default (no file needed): http://localhost:4321
PUBLIC_SITE_ORIGIN=https://shironeshiyaro.github.io

# Keep this in sync with the public site's build when it is deployed under a
# sub-path (for example a GitHub Pages project site): the author shell prefixes
# its links with it exactly like the site does.
# BASE_PATH=/demo/

# Optional test/build seam: read another content root for the shell navigation.
# SELF_PAGE_CONTENT_ROOT=F:\SelfPage\content
